<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <ResourcePreloader />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@@400;700&display=swap" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/BlazorMonaco/lib/monaco-editor/min/vs/editor/editor.main.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="theme.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["SharpNotebook.Web.styles.css"]" />
    <ImportMap />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</head>

<body>
    <!--
    THESIS: SharpNotebook is a calm, dependable dev-tool surface — no theme
    cosplay, no chrome that fights the code. Refuses the "look how retro/edgy
    I am" costume the pixel-art build before it wore.
    OWN-WORLD: Catppuccin Mocha — soft near-black base, one lavender/mauve
    signal color for identity and focus, warm accent set (peach/red/green)
    reserved for state, not decoration. Rounded 8-10px corners, quiet 1px
    borders, soft low-glare shadows — the opposite material of hard pixel
    bevels. Real Monaco editors in every cell, not styled textareas.
    STORY: open a file, trust it if foreign, run cells in a real code editor
    with real completions, read output in a quiet mono readout.
    FIRST VIEWPORT: rounded-panel file browser left; notebook title and
    kernel-lifecycle controls top; cell stack center, each cell its own
    soft-bordered panel holding a Monaco editor.
    FORM: user-pinned direction ("Catppuccin Mocha") — brief overrides the
    roll; supersedes the prior pixel-art world, which is now anti-reference.
    FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with
    the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md.
    -->
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
    <ReconnectModal />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    <script src="_content/BlazorMonaco/jsInterop.js"></script>
    <script src="_content/BlazorMonaco/lib/monaco-editor/min/vs/loader.js"></script>
    <script src="_content/BlazorMonaco/lib/monaco-editor/min/vs/editor/editor.main.js"></script>
    <script src="monaco-ready.js"></script>
    <script src="download.js"></script>
</body>

</html>
